// input: emitted
// FILECHECK-OPTIONS: --implicit-check-not=idr.version --implicit-check-not=idr.entry --implicit-check-not=func.func{{.}}@
// The contract the Idris side emits, in the custom syntax of each dialect.
// The module carries idr.program, and no version, entry or entry kind.
// CHECK: module attributes {{[{][^}]*}}idr.program
// A data type declares its constructors, with the tags Idris gives them
// and their fields. An Idris name is a NameLoc around the source location.
// CHECK: idr.data @Prog.Shape {
// CHECK-DAG: idr.ctor @Circle (i64) {{.*}}loc("Prog.Circle"("Prog.idr":
// CHECK-DAG: idr.ctor @Rect (i64, i64) {{.*}}loc("Prog.Rect"("Prog.idr":
// CHECK: } loc("Prog.Shape"("Prog.idr":
// The root is the only public function; a main : Int program's is () -> i64.
// An erased argument is passed as the erased constant, and a call carries
// its source location.
// CHECK: func.func @Prog.main() -> i64 {
// CHECK-DAG: %[[E:[^ ]+]] = idr.constant #idr.erased : !idr.erased
// CHECK-DAG: idr.con @Prog.Shape::@Rect(%{{[^,]+}}, %{{[^)]+}}) : (i64, i64) -> !idr.data<@Prog.Shape>
// CHECK: func.call @Prog.keep(%[[E]], %{{[^)]+}}) : (!idr.erased, i64) -> i64 loc("Prog.idr":
// CHECK: } loc("Prog.main"("Prog.idr":
// The other functions, in any order: a match on data has one case per
// constructor, its fields the region's arguments; one on an Int matches
// literals. keep and area are total. countdown recurses on an Int: Idris
// does not prove it terminating, so it has no attributes.
// CHECK-DAG: func.func private @Prog.keep(%{{[^:]+}}: !idr.erased, %{{[^:]+}}: i64) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}idr.total
// CHECK-DAG: func.func private @Prog.area(%{{[^:]+}}: !idr.data<@Prog.Shape>) -> i64 attributes {{[{][^}]*}}idr.total
// CHECK-DAG: idr.match %{{[^ ]+}} : !idr.data<@Prog.Shape> -> (i64) {
// CHECK-DAG: case @Circle(%{{[^:]+}}: i64) {
// CHECK-DAG: case @Rect(%{{[^:]+}}: i64, %{{[^:]+}}: i64) {
// CHECK-DAG: func.func private @Prog.countdown(%{{[^:]+}}: i64) -> i64 {{[{]$}}
// CHECK-DAG: idr.match_lit %{{[^ ]+}} : i64 -> (i64) {
